{"path":"iterator/basic_const_iterator","title":"std::basic_const_iterator","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>basic_const_iterator","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/basic_const_iterator","section":"iterator","kind":"page","summary":"std::basic_const_iterator is an iterator adaptor which behaves exactly like the underlying iterator (which must be at least an LegacyInputIterator or model input_iterator), except that dereferencing converts the value returned by the…","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/iterator\">&lt;iterator&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/input_iterator\"><span class=\"kw2882\">std::<span class=\"me2\">input_iterator</span></span></a> Iter <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> basic_const_iterator<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>std::basic_const_iterator</code> is an iterator adaptor which behaves exactly like the underlying iterator (which must be at least an <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/InputIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyInputIterator</em></a> or model <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/input_iterator\"><code>input_iterator</code></a>), except that dereferencing converts the value returned by the underlying iterator as immutable. Specializations of <code>std::basic_const_iterator</code> are constant iterators, that is, the iterator can never be used as an output iterator because modifying elements is not allowed.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Member_types\">Member types</h3>\